1
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,920
Try leaving the light on and stepping away.

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,420
Like someone calling
out to you after the rain.

3
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:35,280
Walking while looking back,
pulled along by the clatter.

4
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:42,300
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:09,100
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

10
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning at that corner.

11
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,780
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari.

13
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:33,020
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:34,540
Thank you.

15
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:39,320
A hellish double date.

16
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:16,960
Impressive, Volvo, a masterful defense!

17
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:23,180
Happy birthday, Bobby,
congratulations on your birthday!

18
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:25,760
Congratulations, Bobby!

19
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:30,120
Did everyone come here for me?

20
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:35,020
Thank you, really, thank you.

21
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:41,400
That was last year's birthday.

22
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:49,180
What a dangerous birthday that was.

23
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:52,020
That was quite a spectacle, wasn't it.

24
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:52,583
Yes,

25
00:02:52,633 --> 00:02:57,540
I wish we could spend this
year's birthday just as merrily.

26
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,980
Throw it! Bombing run!

27
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:11,660
What's this? A dud?

28
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:14,840
It's a message capsule.
It's addressed to Mr. Bobby.

29
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:17,366
Is that really how you send a message?

30
00:03:17,416 --> 00:03:20,520
Your acquaintances are all dangerous types,
aren't they?

31
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:24,960
This one's from Jodie.

32
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,580
What? From Jodie? So what does it say?

33
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:34,049
Well, hi, Bobby.

34
00:03:34,099 --> 00:03:39,260
I'm taking leave and going to
Japan for your birthday next week.

35
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,524
Of course, Daddy doesn't know.

36
00:03:41,574 --> 00:03:44,315
Let's spend a wonderful day together,
just the two of us.

37
00:03:44,365 --> 00:03:45,900
Love, Jodie.

38
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,460
It's not a date invitation.

39
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:50,700
If it's just the two of them,
it won't bother anyone, will it?

40
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:54,880
A whole day alone with Jodie.

41
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:05,420
B-b-bullets!

42
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,300
Bobby!

43
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:12,140
Looks like we're going
to cause a lot of trouble.

44
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,220
I'm such a lucky guy.

45
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:23,980
Ryotsu, have you ever spent a
birthday alone with your girlfriend?

46
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,720
No, sorry, sorry.

47
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:28,840
Asking Ryotsu,
who never gets any girls, was a mistake.

48
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,312
You bastard.

49
00:04:30,362 --> 00:04:33,980
You had zero girls until last year too,
you know.

50
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:44,696
S-somebody...

51
00:04:44,746 --> 00:04:49,040
Somebody help!

52
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:50,880
Where?

53
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:52,580
Barba!

54
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:53,680
W-wait!

55
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,900
Nobody's coming to help.

56
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:58,000
So it really is this much

57
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,180
Wait.

58
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,080
What?

59
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:03,540
What?

60
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,560
Just as expected of a Volvo.

61
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:28,380
There was no room for me to step in

62
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:31,760
Are you hurt?

63
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:32,600
Thank you.

64
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:34,620
for saving us.

65
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:36,340
Cut, cut, cut!

66
00:05:37,580 --> 00:05:38,860
Come on, you guys, this is a problem.

67
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:40,340
This scene is totally ruined now.

68
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,960
So it was a movie shoot?

69
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:43,820
Movie.

70
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:46,160
Why is Maria in the movie?

71
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,040
No, that's not me.

72
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,360
That's not me.

73
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:50,000
What?

74
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,900
Two Marias?

75
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,000
That one's Marilyn.

76
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,000
She's a huge star.

77
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,280
Her real name is Asatorin.

78
00:05:58,280 --> 00:06:00,280
She's my twin sister.

79
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,720
Sister? Actress?

80
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:04,660
The ones you took down were

81
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:07,280
top martial artists, even in Hong Kong!

82
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:10,940
I love strong people!

83
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,560
So you're her sister?

84
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:16,000
And these squishy breasts?

85
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,940
Of course, unlike Maria,
these are the real thing!

86
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,160
See?

87
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:23,660
How bold!

88
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:26,960
My sister is very forward about everything.

89
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:29,780
W-wow, this is... too much!

90
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:37,640
Let's see, Hong Kong superstar
Marilyn boldly declares she has a lover!

91
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:42,300
The lucky man is civil servant Mr. Volvo,
I presume?

92
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:43,460
How bold.

93
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:44,920
Well, that's

94
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,720
You're popular, Volvo!

95
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:50,480
Why don't you just marry Marilyn?

96
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:52,600
D-don't be stupid!

97
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:02,780
Maybe marrying Marilyn
wouldn't be so bad either.

98
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:05,120
Watch out, Volvo!

99
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:10,140
Volvo, are you okay?

100
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:13,340
It came in through the same hole as before,
exactly.

101
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:15,260
That's why I said it was dangerous.

102
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:17,380
I let my guard down, which is unlike me.

103
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,740
It's from Jodie again.

104
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:21,240
I wonder what it is this time.

105
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:22,480
This is...

106
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:25,300
This? Look! It's the birthday plan!

107
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,400
So she really thought it through.

108
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:31,400
How thoughtful.
She'll make a wonderful wife.

109
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:33,540
Y-you think so?

110
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:44,060
Maybe marrying Jodie
really is the better choice.

111
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:48,500
A date at the fitness club pool is just right for you two,
isn't it?

112
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:50,060
What? A pool?

113
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:53,640
Yes, well,
it's written right there in Jodie's letter.

114
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,440
So that means...

115
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:07,520
I-I can't stop!

116
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:13,400
At this rate,
marriage is still a long way off.

117
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:14,100
Yeah.

118
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,220
Someone's there.

119
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:32,220
Marilyn!

120
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,000
Welcome back.

121
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,200
I've been waiting for you.

122
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:37,300
Let's hurry and go inside.

123
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:47,720
Bobby, you're so impatient.

124
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,680
This is

125
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:50,660
Excuse me.

126
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:52,620
But this is...

127
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:56,260
Marilyn!

128
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:58,080
That outfit...

129
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:01,200
Of course I got it ready for Bobby.

130
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:03,000
How do I look?

131
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:09,300
Bobby, are you all right?

132
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:10,580
Lin

133
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:12,840
So you were here after all.

134
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:15,560
The film crew came all the
way to my house looking for you.

135
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:19,160
What do you think you're doing,
causing everyone this trouble?

136
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:21,120
Okay, okay, I get it already.

137
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:28,440
Hey, Bobby,
what are these marks on this calendar?

138
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:31,560
It's my birthday.

139
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:32,860
I see.

140
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:35,460
Then let's spend that
day just the two of us.

141
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:37,320
Understood.

142
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,480
Then I'm looking forward to it.

143
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,840
Good night, Bobby.

144
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,680
G-good night.

145
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:50,700
If she keeps pressing me like that on my birthday too,
I won't survive.

146
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:54,580
Didn't something happen on my birthday...?

147
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,660
What a sinful man I am.

148
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:06,988
Without even realizing it,

149
00:10:07,038 --> 00:10:10,040
I've been toying with two maidens' hearts.

150
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:14,800
Aren't you just blinded by Marilyn's
charm and forgot your promise to Jodie?

151
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,070
Lucky you,

152
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:21,520
Ryotsu, you've never had to
deal with worries like this,

153
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:24,720
you were no different just a year ago,
were you?

154
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:29,820
I just happened to work in
a place with no women around,

155
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:33,260
so I must have had the appeal all along.

156
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:36,720
I ought to strangle you, you bastard.

157
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:42,400
Mr. Nakagawa, as two popular men,
could you give me some advice?

158
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:44,060
Y-yeah.

159
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:48,440
I don't want to see Jolly or Marie cry,
either one of them.

160
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:51,960
I think my little sister would get
really angry before she cries, though.

161
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:53,960
She'd get angry?

162
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:56,800
Yes, my sister has a fierce temper.

163
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,480
The martial arts they used in the
movie were pretty authentic, too.

164
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:01,260
Of course they're the real thing.

165
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:06,340
We've trained in every kind of
martial art together since we were kids.

166
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:08,940
An angry little sister is scary, you know.

167
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:12,560
After all, she's strong enough to have
knocked down a cow with her bare hands.

168
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:20,100
I see.

169
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:31,260
If you turn down Marilyn's invitation,

170
00:11:31,260 --> 00:11:34,060
you'll meet the same fate as the cow.

171
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:35,660
Th-that's right.

172
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:39,680
Jodie can only stay in Japan during the location shoot,
after all.

173
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,620
Naturally,
we should give priority to her schedule.

174
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:46,280
But isn't Jodie scary too when she's angry?

175
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:50,000
I heard she once knocked down a bear with her bare hands,
didn't I?

176
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:52,060
A bear!?

177
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:15,240
Ho ho, so if I turn down Jodie's invitation,
I'll end up with the same fate as Kuma-san?

178
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,780
Being a popular man has
its own share of troubles

179
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:21,740
What on earth am I
supposed to do about this?

180
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:27,520
Tell me, Mr. Nakagawa.
You're popular, so you should know.

181
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:30,980
I've never dated a
woman that amazing either.

182
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:33,580
At this point,
even an unpopular Ryotsu will do.

183
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:35,460
Somehow, just do something!

184
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:39,580
Well, unpopular men might
as well go play pachinko.

185
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,920
Pick whichever you like, cow or bear.

186
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:44,800
How heartless!

187
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:47,140
Wait.

188
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:52,460
This might be a good chance to
make that handsome Bobby suffer.

189
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:53,980
Alright, I understand.

190
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:55,940
And it's Volvo asking, of all people.

191
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:57,680
Leave everything to me.

192
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:58,880
Really?

193
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,060
Yeah, really.

194
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:01,540
Thank you, Ryotsu.

195
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:02,840
I'll owe you one.

196
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:08,160
Enjoy your happiness while you can.

197
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:14,780
Listen up.

198
00:13:14,780 --> 00:13:18,220
This is the fitness club
where Jodie is waiting.

199
00:13:19,060 --> 00:13:22,480
And this is the Chinese restaurant
where Marilyn chose to eat.

200
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:25,500
Using this route,
it's about two minutes by car.

201
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:29,040
It's entirely possible to date
both of them at the same time.

202
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,860
So a double date is an option after all.

203
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:36,300
Over there, I've loaded all the
props we'll need for the dates.

204
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:41,420
I also had Nakagawa gather costumes
to handle any situation we might face.

205
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:43,400
Nakagawa really is something, isn't he.

206
00:13:46,180 --> 00:13:48,340
By the way,
something's been bugging me since earlier.

207
00:13:48,820 --> 00:13:50,380
Why do we have a video camera?

208
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:53,340
Well, I don't really know either,

209
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:56,460
but the senior officer
told me to film the date.

210
00:13:56,460 --> 00:14:00,860
A double date is like talking
to two different people at once.

211
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:05,400
Going back and forth, you can lose track of
which one you were talking to and what you said.

212
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:07,760
That's when you check with this video.

213
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:08,480
I see.

214
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:12,000
Though it might have other uses too.

215
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:16,220
You've never even been on a double date,
yet you think of all this?

216
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:17,340
Well, sorry about that.

217
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:20,020
Senior officer,
we're almost at the fitness club.

218
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:24,160
Now the hellish double date begins!

219
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,540
H-hey, Johnny

220
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:37,240
Bobby

221
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,660
Johnny

222
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:42,280
It's finally starting, the shoot begins!

223
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:42,760
Yes.

224
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,640
Th-this is...

225
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:52,480
It's a swimsuit I specially
prepared for your birthday.

226
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:53,940
Does it suit me?

227
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:56,400
I'm overwhelmed!

228
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,020
Bobby, are you all right?

229
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:01,980
This closeness is irresistible again!

230
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,223
Shinopool, you mean?

231
00:15:07,273 --> 00:15:10,320
It was one of the seven
mysteries at my elementary school.

232
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:14,440
Ours too.
I never thought I'd actually see it.

233
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:17,080
Frutta, it's me!

234
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:20,160
Marilyn just walked into the shop.

235
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:22,200
Got it. Come over right away.

236
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:22,760
Yes.

237
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:28,340
You can stay like this until you calm down.

238
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:30,660
Thank you, Jodie.

239
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:33,840
Sweet Jodie.

240
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:37,220
You'll keep doing this even
after we're married, right?

241
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:41,180
I'm the happiest man in the world.

242
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:45,260
What's wrong, Bobby?

243
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:46,600
Bobby...

244
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:48,240
It's nothing.

245
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:50,780
I'm going to take a short
break in the infirmary.

246
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,680
Then I'll come too.

247
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:55,860
No, I'll be right back, so wait for me.

248
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:04,100
That place won't let you in
unless you're wearing a tie.

249
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:04,920
Got it.

250
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:10,440
Welcome!

251
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,460
Volvo Saigo-sama, is it?

252
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:13,100
That's right.

253
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:14,000
Bobby

254
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:21,500
I prepared a special dress for today's date.

255
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:25,540
Wow, this is unbearable!

256
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,300
What's wrong, Bobby?

257
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:32,700
N-nothing, it's just really quiet, isn't it?

258
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:36,220
This restaurant,
it's like we're the only customers here.

259
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:38,290
I had the place reserved for us today.

260
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:41,220
Because I wanted to spend
time alone with Bobby.

261
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,860
T-this chest feeling...

262
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,400
It's irresistible!

263
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:49,720
It's a ceiling with a pattern of dyed earth,
you know.

264
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:52,020
If it were summer, that'd be a stairs gag.

265
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:54,280
It's me!

266
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:57,860
This is bad.
Jodie has started looking for Volvo.

267
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:01,720
Come on, eat up.

268
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:03,540
This looks delicious.

269
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,360
Here you go, Bobby.

270
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:07,860
Th-thank you.

271
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:15,840
Marilyn is so kind, I bet she'll keep
doing this even after we're married.

272
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:19,240
I'm the luckiest man in the universe.

273
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:22,960
Bobby, what's wrong?

274
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:26,560
It's nothing.
I'm just going to the restroom for a moment.

275
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:30,480
Hurry up, Jodie's waiting for you!

276
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:33,060
Shall we make our move now?

277
00:17:35,980 --> 00:17:37,820
Nakagawa, the videotape is about to run out!

278
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:41,160
There should be a convenience store over there.
Go buy a new one right away.

279
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:42,480
I'll keep an eye on the car.

280
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:43,420
Understood.

281
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:51,900
There's a car illegally parked
in front of the Press Club.

282
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:53,880
Couldn't they just tow that nuisance away?

283
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:00,740
Sorry.

284
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:02,980
The moment I looked away,

285
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:04,860
it got towed!

286
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:05,780
No way.

287
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,860
How are we supposed to get
to the Chinese restaurant now?

288
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:10,600
Looks like we'll have to run.

289
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,300
What about our clothes?

290
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:14,340
It's a place that requires proper attire.

291
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,100
Borrow some from Nakagawa.

292
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:18,420
Nakagawa, go with him.

293
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:19,380
Yes, understood.

294
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:20,340
Well then, let's go.

295
00:18:20,340 --> 00:18:20,700
Alright.

296
00:18:21,340 --> 00:18:23,260
What should I do?

297
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:24,980
You're going with Volvo and the others too.

298
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:28,180
But leave the recorded tape behind.

299
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:29,740
Why?

300
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:32,700
Excuse me.

301
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:34,340
I'm not a suspicious person.

302
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:37,040
Hey there.

303
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:39,160
Sorry to keep you waiting.

304
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,580
Bobby, what happened to your outfit?

305
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,740
It's nothing serious.

306
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:52,260
Bobby, honestly...

307
00:18:52,260 --> 00:18:53,600
Jodie.

308
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:55,020
What a coincidence.

309
00:18:55,020 --> 00:18:56,180
What are you doing here?

310
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:58,840
Bobby disappeared in the middle of our date!

311
00:18:58,840 --> 00:18:59,600
What?

312
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:02,000
So he was on a date with you too?

313
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,420
Uh-oh.

314
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:04,840
With you too.

315
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:06,380
What do you mean by that?

316
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:08,180
Just forget I said anything.

317
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:11,980
What's that tape?

318
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:12,700
This is...

319
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,260
Now you understand, don't you?

320
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:24,280
The truth is, that Volvo guy has
been two-timing Jodie and this woman.

321
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:25,620
What did you say?

322
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:29,840
To him, women are just playthings.

323
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:33,460
I can't forgive this.
I absolutely can't forgive him!

324
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:34,980
He took the bait.

325
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:37,900
Miss Marilyn, you have a phone call.

326
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:39,660
I see.

327
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:40,840
This way, please.

328
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:42,480
You...

329
00:19:44,420 --> 00:19:47,814
We have something to tell you.
These two were in cahoots,

330
00:19:47,864 --> 00:19:50,915
and were trying to squeeze
every penny out of you.

331
00:19:50,965 --> 00:19:52,860
They're a pair of real scoundrels.

332
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:57,220
Unforgivable.
I absolutely won't forgive him!

333
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:00,260
That settles Volvo's fate.

334
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:02,940
You're the enemy of all women!

335
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,400
How dare you deceive me!

336
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:09,080
Serves you right for playing the
lady-killer and making a fool of me.

337
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:11,460
W-what?

338
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:23,880
Jodie

339
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:27,200
I never expected you'd barge in here.

340
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:32,660
Jodie, there's a perfectly
good reason for this.

341
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:38,180
Go for it, Jodie!

342
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:39,940
Do what you like, I'll allow it.

343
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,580
Poor Bobby.

344
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:46,000
You've been fooled, haven't you?

345
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:51,980
Let's get out of here right
now and redo the birthday party.

346
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:53,860
How did it come to this?

347
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:57,900
Who are you calling a little vixen?

348
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:03,820
You're the real villain here,
trying to drag Bobby down the path of evil!

349
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,220
I won't let Bobby go to someone like you!

350
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:09,240
Bobby is mine!

351
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:10,600
Don't give him up!

352
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:11,880
Grr, you!

353
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:15,400
That's it!
Just keep at it and finish her off!

354
00:21:19,660 --> 00:21:20,920
Ugh, pin her down!

355
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,700
Let go of me!

356
00:21:24,860 --> 00:21:26,520
You let go first!

357
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:34,340
What about you?

358
00:21:41,660 --> 00:21:44,700
Aaargh! If it's come to this...

359
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:48,880
Then I'll have to take you down, you there!

360
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:50,540
Aaaaah!

361
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,920
What a fierce fight.

362
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:09,500
Just what you'd expect
from a bear and a cow.

363
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:20,820
What are you two fighting for?

364
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:22,780
Your enemy is Volvo, you know!

365
00:22:22,780 --> 00:22:23,740
Shut up!

366
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:36,100
Even one of them alone is a handful.

367
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:39,760
Ajie!

368
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:49,320
Help me!

369
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,420
Somebody help me!

370
00:23:10,860 --> 00:23:13,320
How did it come to this?

371
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:13,340
Why?

372
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:17,380
Bobby? Where are you? Bobby!

373
00:23:21,820 --> 00:23:22,480
What's that?

374
00:23:24,060 --> 00:23:27,060
I'm taking Bobby with me! Bye!

375
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:31,740
She even prepared something like that.

376
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:34,300
Just as expected of Hong Kong's top actress.

377
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:35,940
Goddamn it!

378
00:23:36,280 --> 00:23:39,660
Even if he's at the ends of the earth,
I'll get Bobby back!

379
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:46,280
Thank you for watching.

